# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Innocent — what git must never see.
#
# The first block is the one that matters. A build artefact committed by
# mistake is noise; a signing key committed by mistake is permanent. Git keeps
# every version of every file forever, and deleting it later does not remove
# it from forks, clones, or any CI log that printed it. There is no undo.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# SIGNING — never, under any circumstances
*.jks
*.keystore
*.p12
*.pem
android/key.properties
android/signing.properties
android/app/innocent.jks

# Local machine paths, not portable
android/local.properties
android/.gradle/
.metadata

# Build output — regenerated every time, and large
build/
android/app/build/
.dart_tool/
.flutter-plugins
.flutter-plugins-dependencies
.packages
*.apk
*.aab

# Generated by `flutter pub get` / the build, and regenerated on demand.
#
# Every one of these reappears the moment anyone runs `flutter pub get`, so
# leaving them visible means `git status` is never clean and a real change is
# harder to spot in the noise. None of them is authored by hand; all of them
# are reproducible from files that ARE committed.
#
# pubspec.lock is the one with a trade-off. Dart's advice for an APPLICATION
# is to commit it, so every build resolves the same dependency versions. This
# repo has never committed it — CI has always resolved fresh — so ignoring it
# changes nothing today. If reproducible builds ever matter more than the
# quiet status, delete this line and commit the lock; the two cannot both be
# true.
pubspec.lock

# The l10n generator's output. `lib/l10n/*.arb` are the SOURCES and stay
# committed; these .dart files are produced from them by `flutter pub get`
# (pubspec has `generate: true`).
lib/l10n/app_localizations.dart
lib/l10n/app_localizations_*.dart

# Flutter's plugin registrars, on both platforms. Matches Flutter's own
# default template. GeneratedPluginRegistrant.m/.h were previously COMMITTED
# and are untracked by the same change that added these lines — they are
# rewritten by every `pub get`, so keeping them tracked meant a diff on every
# dependency change that nobody ever read.
ios/Flutter/
ios/Runner/GeneratedPluginRegistrant.*
android/app/src/main/java/io/flutter/plugins/GeneratedPluginRegistrant.java
android/app/src/main/java/

# Editors
.idea/
.vscode/
*.iml

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# NOTE: android/app/libs/*.aar are NOT ignored and must stay committed.
# They are the iADB helper libraries, they have no public Maven coordinates,
# and the build fails without them. Four files, ~120 KB total.
